## ApacheCon@Home - Tracks

### Keynote Presentations

Each day starts at 13:00 UTC with introductory remarks from Rich Bowen, VP Conferences at the Apache Software Foundation

#### Tuesday, September 21

- 13:00 UTC - Welcome remarks and State of the Feather
- 13:30 UTC - Ashley Wolf - The Inclusive Community Imperative (and where the next 50 million developers will come from)
- 13:45 UTC - Apurva Desai (Google) - Open Data Lakes: Latest stop in the big data journey

<a class="btn" href="/events/apachecon-home-2021/tracks/keynotes">Details</a>

#### Wednesday, September 22

- 13:00 UTC - Opening remarks
- 13:15 UTC - Mark Cox - community-led security at asf
- 13:30 UTC - Anil Inamdar (Instaclustr) - Open Core Vs Open Source
- 13:45 UTC - Willem Jiang (Huawei) - Open Source Community -- The Utopia for Programmers

<a class="btn" href="/events/apachecon-home-2021/tracks/keynotes">Details</a>

#### Thursday, September 23

- 13:00 UTC - Opening remarks
- 13:15 UTC - Alison Parker, Michael Weinberg - Open Hardware vs. COVID-19
- 13:30 UTC - Mark Shan (Tencent): Apache Way in Tencent

<a class="btn" href="/events/apachecon-home-2021/tracks/keynotes">Details</a>

